From: ultimatejeeves <ultimatejeeves@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:47:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 13/43] JIT: persistent compiled code cache for the page

Compiling a block is ~2/3 Jitter and ~1/3 V8 compiling the wasm. Blocks are keyed by XXH3-128 over
their instructions, address range, category, compile hints and a per-type salt (EE: FP rounding mode
and idle-loop flags, which read code outside the block); VU blocks aren't cached. The page loads
stored entries before booting (jitCacheAlloc/jitCacheLoad) and takes new ones (jitCacheTakeNew);
a hit skips the Jitter. Verify mode compiles anyway and compares: 0 mismatches over 13,837 hits.

THPS4, 40 s from a save state: 4.06 s of compiling -> 1.75 s, worst frame 1.9 s -> 0.7 s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
